\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.2}{\ignorespaces Two readings of a steep yield curve. Forward rates above short rates can mean that short rates will rise, as the expectations hypothesis says, or that long bonds will earn more than short ones, a term premium. The tests in this chapter measure how much of each.}}{85}{figure.caption.24}\protected@file@percent }
